// Title: Sysmon Configuration Update
// Sigma ID: 87911521-7098-470b-a459-9a57fc80bdfd
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2023-03-09 | Modified: 2026-06-29
// ATT&CK: defense-impairment, T1685
// Description: Detects updates to Sysmon's configuration. Attackers might update or replace the Sysmon
//   configuration with a bare bone one to avoid monitoring without shutting down the service
//   completely
// False positives:
//   - Legitimate administrators might use this command to update Sysmon configuration.
// References:
//   - https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/sysinternals/downloads/sysmon
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/ad147b5514596e70f2782769d9833046b7c8e12b/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_sysinternals_sysmon_config_update.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language, Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where ((FolderPath endswith "\\Sysmon64.exe" or FolderPath endswith "\\Sysmon64a.exe" or FolderPath endswith "\\Sysmon.exe") or ProcessVersionInfoFileDescription =~ "System activity monitor") and (ProcessCommandLine contains "-c" or ProcessCommandLine contains "/c" or ProcessCommandLine contains "–c" or ProcessCommandLine contains "—c" or ProcessCommandLine contains "―c")
